## Step 8 — Test It

```bash
# Get the public load balancer address (takes 2-3 min to appear)
kubectl get service my-microservice

# Once EXTERNAL-IP shows a hostname (not <pending>):
curl http://<EXTERNAL-IP>
```

Expected response:
```json
{"message":"Hello from my microservice on EKS!","hostname":"my-microservice-xxxx"}
```

Run curl a few times — the `hostname` changes between your two pods, proving the load balancer distributes traffic.

