## Step 10 — Clean Up (Avoid Surprise Bills)

```bash
# Delete the app first — this removes the load balancer
kubectl delete -f deployment.yaml

# Delete the cluster
eksctl delete cluster --name demo-test --region ap-south-1

# Delete the image repository (optional)
aws ecr delete-repository --repository-name my-microservice --region ap-south-1 --force
```

> ⚠️ Always delete the Service/LoadBalancer BEFORE deleting the cluster.
> If you skip this, the load balancer stays alive in AWS and keeps billing you.

